{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1523979672,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM4MjAzOTcxNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2281#issuecomment-382039717"},"message":"Sorry, I  missed this issue.  I just came across it when searching for something else.\n\n`git submodule deinit` barfs because datalad creates \"old-form\" submodules (to use the phrase from `man gitsubmodules`) rather than those that are gitlinks to .git/modules/.  In any case, IIUC what you're after, that wouldn't do what you want because it clears the subds directory rather than unregistering it as submodule.\n\nBut, if you reverse your proposed steps above, I think you get what you want:\n\n```bash\n$\u003e mv subds{,.aside} \u0026\u0026 datalad remove -d. -m\"unregister subds\" -r subds\n```\n\n---\n\nA more complete snippet:\n\n```bash\n$\u003e datalad create /tmp/dl-2281\n$\u003e cd /tmp/dl-2281\n$\u003e echo 1 \u003efoo\n$\u003e datalad add .\n\n$\u003e datalad create -d. subds\n$\u003e cd subds\n$\u003e echo 2 \u003ebar\n$\u003e datalad add .\n$\u003e cd ..\n\n$\u003e git submodule\n+24579372567b6e586d09448658dc19c44221b4dd subds (heads/master)\n$\u003e tree\n.\n├── foo -\u003e .git/annex/objects/06/7v/MD5E-s2--b026324c6904b2a9cb4b88d6d61c81d1/MD5E-s2--b026324c6904b2a9cb4b88d6d61c81d1\n└── subds\n    └── bar -\u003e .git/annex/objects/GK/31/MD5E-s2--26ab0db90d72e28ad0ba1e22ee510510/MD5E-s2--26ab0db90d72e28ad0ba1e22ee510510\n\n1 directory, 2 files\n\n$\u003e mv subds{,.aside}\n$\u003e datalad remove -d. -m\"unregister subds\" -r subds\n$\u003e git submodule\n$\u003e tree\n.\n├── foo -\u003e .git/annex/objects/06/7v/MD5E-s2--b026324c6904b2a9cb4b88d6d61c81d1/MD5E-s2--b026324c6904b2a9cb4b88d6d61c81d1\n└── subds.aside\n    └── bar -\u003e .git/annex/objects/GK/31/MD5E-s2--26ab0db90d72e28ad0ba1e22ee510510/MD5E-s2--26ab0db90d72e28ad0ba1e22ee510510\n\n1 directory, 2 files\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1524226149,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM4MzA3NTg4OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2281#issuecomment-383075888"},"message":"I'll close this because `mv subds{,.aside} \u0026\u0026 datalad remove -d. -m\"unregister subds\" -r subds` does what you want, I think, and it's as short as your proposed sequence.  Please reopen if it doesn't work for you.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1524226149,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTU4NjAxMzQwNw=="},"status":2}]}